    "text": "Excess of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaOH</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo></math> was added to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>FeCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>aq</mi></mfenced></math> resulting into <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Fe</mi><msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>OH</mi></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msub></math>. The molarity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>FeCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>aq</mi></mfenced></math> is:<br /><br />(Given the molar mass of<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Fe</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and molar mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cl</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>35</mn><mo>.5</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)"
